  intro={`
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Leighton is a small Colbert County community on the Tennessee River, connected to the broader Shoals market by US-72 and the river corridor that has defined this part of Alabama for generations. It's a community of working families, agricultural landowners, and retirees who've lived in Colbert County their entire lives — a customer base that responds to dependability, honest dealing, and a company that doesn't treat a smaller market as a second priority.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Leighton and the surrounding Colbert County communities — Cherokee, Barton, the unincorporated areas between the Shoals cities — have homes that are largely crawlspace construction from the 1950s through 1990s, sitting on the river valley clay soil that creates persistent moisture management challenges. These are the homes where we find the most significant crawlspace mold on inspection — not because the homeowners are negligent, but because the construction era, the soil type, and the regional humidity create conditions that build toward mold growth over decades, quietly and invisibly.</p>
